omega_sources='''<div class="source-list"><a class="card" href="https://lpscpubvalence.lpsc.louisiana.gov/portal/PSC/DocketDetails?docketId=32146" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>LOUISIANA PUBLIC SERVICE COMMISSION</span><h3>Docket U-37882</h3><p>Entergy Louisiana’s application for generation and transmission resources connected to the North Louisiana data-center project.</p></a><a class="card" href="https://lpscpubvalence.lpsc.louisiana.gov/portal/PSC/DocumentDetails?documentId=180141" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>LPSC ORDER</span><h3>Order No. U-37882</h3><p>Procedural order establishing the evidentiary record and schedule for Commission consideration.</p></a><a class="card" href="https://lpscpubvalence.lpsc.louisiana.gov/portal/PSC/ViewFile?fileId=kt5JixLAYFY%3D" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>PUBLIC FILING</span><h3>Transmission project testimony</h3><p>Public testimony describing the West Fork Creek–St. Landry 500-kV line and related facilities.</p></a><a class="card" href="https://www.entergy.com/news/entergy-louisiana-announces-a-new-agreement-with-meta-that-will-deliver-an-additional-2b-in-customer-savings" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>ENTERGY</span><h3>Project announcement</h3><p>Entergy’s announcement of the broader infrastructure buildout supporting Meta’s North Louisiana data center.</p></a><a class="card" href="https://www.kalb.com/2026/10/03/louisiana-landowners-oppose-transmission-line-meant-support-metas-data-center-entergy-attempts-quell-concerns/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>PROJECT OMEGA · LOCAL REPORT</span><h3>October 2 route map and project timeline</h3><p>Local reporting includes the route graphic and project timeline distributed at the October 1 landowner meeting. Confirm any parcel against current records.</p></a></div>'''
page('/west-fork-creek','West Fork Creek–Boeuf 500-kV Transmission Project | Project Omega','Information for Louisiana landowners about the proposed West Fork Creek transmission corridor through LaSalle and neighboring parishes.','''<section class="hero"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">LaSalle · Rapides · Avoyelles · Caldwell · Richland</p><h1>West Fork Creek–Boeuf<br>500-kV Transmission Project</h1><p class="lede">Project Omega is the public name being used for the proposed high-voltage transmission corridor connecting the West Fork Creek area toward the North Louisiana data-center development.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/book-online">Request a property-rights review</a><a class="button secondary" href="#records">View the public record</a></div><p class="fine">Entergy / expropriation inquiries: <a href="tel:+15043772620">504-377-2620</a></p></div></section><section class="wrap omega-video"><p class="eyebrow">PROJECT OMEGA IN THE NEWS</p><h2 id="omega-video-title">LaSalle Parish landowner shares concerns in KLTV report</h2><p>The October 3 report covers the proposed West Fork Creek–Boeuf line. Its caption identifies Richland and Rapides parishes; the interview includes a LaSalle Parish landowner. This is Project Omega coverage, not the separate Babel–Webre project.</p><div class="video-frame"><iframe title="KLTV video: Louisiana landowners oppose transmission line meant to support Meta’s data center" src="https://gray.video-player.arcpublishing.com/prod/powaEmbed.html?org=gray&amp;uuid=6555e101-9c54-4a72-bb8f-03e6bed45f28&amp;powa-promo=default" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy" allow="autoplay; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture; fullscreen" allowfullscreen referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"></iframe></div><p class="muted">Video by KLTV / Gray Media · Published October 3, 2026 · <a href="https://www.kltv.com/video/2026/10/03/louisiana-landowners-oppose-transmission-line-meant-support-metas-data-center/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the original story</a>.</p><p><a href="/west-fork-creek/news">See all Project Omega news and coverage →</a></p></section><section class="wrap prose"><p class="eyebrow">What the records show</p><h2>One project, several names.</h2><p>Public reporting and landowner route materials refer to the corridor as the <strong>West Fork Creek–Boeuf 500-kV Transmission Project</strong> or <strong>Project Omega</strong>. The Louisiana Public Service Commission filings use the related description <strong>West Fork Creek–St. Landry 500 kV</strong> within the broader Evest/Meta infrastructure case, LPSC Docket U-37882.</p><p>Because route descriptions and engineering plans can change, a parcel should be evaluated against the current route materials—not against a general project summary or a verbal description alone.</p><h2>How we work with landowners</h2><div class="cards"><article class="card"><h3>1. Start with your documents</h3><p>We review the project notice, route materials, survey communications, offer, appraisal, and any proposed right-of-way agreement you provide.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>2. Focus on your property</h3><p>We identify the rights being requested and the property-specific impacts that the available records support.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>3. Explain the choices</h3><p>We discuss the available next steps, the proposed scope of work, fees, and expenses in writing before representation begins. You decide whether to proceed.</p></article></div><div class="callout"><strong>Clear starting point.</strong><p>When a written engagement uses a Protected Baseline, the existing offer is identified as the starting reference and the agreement explains how it is treated in evaluating any additional recovery and fees. The terms are set out for that matter in writing.</p></div><div class="callout"><strong>Keep the projects and maps separate.</strong><p>Project Omega / West Fork Creek–Boeuf is the North Louisiana corridor discussed here. Babel–Webre is a different 500-kV project on a separate route. Some parish names overlap, but their route maps and parcel lists are not interchangeable. <a href="https://entergybabelwebre.winchlawfirm.com/">View the separate Babel–Webre project page.</a> Always check the latest project-specific route materials.</p></div><div class="callout"><strong>If surveyors, acquisition agents, or Entergy representatives have contacted you, preserve every letter, map, survey notice, offer, appraisal, and right-of-way document.</strong><br><a href="/book-online">Ask the firm to review the materials.</a></div></section><section class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Public documents & links</p><h2 id="records">Start with the record.</h2><p class="muted">These links open the public sources currently identified for the project. LPSC filings may include public redactions and separate exhibits.</p>'''+omega_sources+'''</section><section class="wrap band"><h2>Is your property near the proposed corridor?</h2><p>The existence of a proposed route does not answer what rights may be acquired, what interests may be affected, or what compensation may be owed. Those questions turn on the documents and the property.</p><a class="button" href="/book-online">Request a consultation</a></section>''')
page('/west-fork-creek/news','Project Omega News & Coverage | Winch Law Firm','A curated hub of news coverage and public information about the West Fork Creek–Boeuf / Project Omega transmission project.','''<section class="wrap prose"><p class="eyebrow">WEST FORK CREEK–BOEUF · PROJECT OMEGA</p><h1>Project news &amp; coverage</h1><p>Coverage and public materials about the proposed North Louisiana corridor, collected in one place. News reports are third-party accounts; route details can change. Verify a parcel against current project and regulatory records.</p><div class="callout"><strong>Project check:</strong> This page covers Project Omega / West Fork Creek–Boeuf. It is separate from Babel–Webre, which has its own page and route map.</div></section><section class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">FEATURED VIDEO</p><h2>KLTV: Louisiana landowners oppose transmission line</h2><p>Published October 3, 2026. The report caption references Richland and Rapides parishes; the video includes a LaSalle Parish landowner.</p><div class="video-frame"><iframe title="KLTV video: Louisiana landowners oppose transmission line meant to support Meta’s data center" src="https://gray.video-player.arcpublishing.com/prod/powaEmbed.html?org=gray&amp;uuid=6555e101-9c54-4a72-bb8f-03e6bed45f28&amp;powa-promo=default" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy" allow="autoplay; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture; fullscreen" allowfullscreen referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"></iframe></div><p class="muted"><a href="https://www.kltv.com/video/2026/10/03/louisiana-landowners-oppose-transmission-line-meant-support-metas-data-center/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open KLTV’s original story</a>.</p></section><section class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">NEWS REPORTS</p><h2>Coverage by publication date</h2><div class="source-list"><a class="card" href="https://www.kltv.com/video/2026/10/03/louisiana-landowners-oppose-transmission-line-meant-support-metas-data-center/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>KLTV · OCT. 3, 2026</span><h3>Louisiana landowners oppose transmission line meant to support Meta’s data center</h3><p>Video report. Its caption mentions Richland and Rapides parishes; the interview includes a LaSalle Parish landowner.</p></a><a class="card" href="https://www.kalb.com/2026/10/03/louisiana-landowners-oppose-transmission-line-meant-support-metas-data-center-entergy-attempts-quell-concerns/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>KALB · OCT. 3, 2026</span><h3>Landowner concerns and the proposed route</h3><p>Related local coverage with the project map and process materials shown at the October 1 meeting.</p></a><a class="card" href="https://www.aol.com/articles/people-tell-entergy-dont-want-194634000.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>ALEXANDRIA TOWN TALK · OCT. 2, 2026</span><h3>People tell Entergy they don’t want the Meta power line on their property</h3><p>Reporting on the proposed corridor and landowner questions across five parishes.</p></a><a class="card" href="https://rapidesparishjournal.com/2026/09/14/omega-routing-a-revelation-to-landowners/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>RAPIDES PARISH JOURNAL · SEPT. 14, 2026</span><h3>Omega routing a revelation to landowners</h3><p>Local reporting and a map attributed to a public service commissioner, through The Jena Times.</p></a><a class="card" href="https://www.therichlandbeaconnews.com/article/1675,frustrated-landowners-form-statewide-coalition-to-fight-entergy-transmission-line" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>THE RICHLAND BEACON-NEWS · SEPT. 3, 2026</span><h3>Landowners form a statewide coalition</h3><p>Coverage of landowner organizing and reported communities along the proposed route.</p></a></div></section><section class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">PRIMARY MATERIALS</p><h2>Check the public record</h2><p>Regulatory filings and project documents are the place to verify current project facts and route changes.</p>'''+omega_sources+'''</section><section class="wrap band"><h2>Have a project notice or property-specific question?</h2><p>Keep the correspondence, map, survey notice, offer, and appraisal together. A project-wide article cannot establish what a particular parcel may face.</p><a class="button" href="/book-online">Request a property-rights review</a></section>''')
